 I was rejoiced to hear, for it was childlike and full of hilarity, said it was n…”"},{"id":"mr-swiveller","name":"Mr. Swiveller","aliases":["Swiveller"],"role":"major","group":"g-swiveller","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “It’s Dick Swiveller,’ said the young fellow, pushing him in.”"},{"id":"nell","name":"Nell","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “What if I had lost thee, Nell!’”"},{"id":"dick","name":"Dick","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “‘No, but IS he?’ said Dick.”"},{"id":"richard-swiveller","name":"Richard Swiveller","aliases":["Mr. Richard","Richard","Mr. Richard Swiveller"],"role":"major","group":"g-swiveller","firstAppearance":"s7","summary":"First mention: “Mr Richard Swiveller’s apartments were in the neighbourhood of Drury Lane, and in addition to this convenience of situation had the advantage of being over a tobacconist’s shop, so that he was enabled to procure a ref…”"},{"id":"sally-brass","name":"Sally Brass","aliases":["Miss Sally","Sally","Miss Sally Brass"],"role":"major","group":"g-brass","firstAppearance":"s33","summary":"First mention: “Miss Sally Brass, then, was a lady of thirty-five or thereabouts, of a gaunt and bony figure, and a resolute bearing, which if it repressed the softer emotions of love, and kept admirers at a distance, certainly inspi…”"},{"id":"barbara","name":"Barbara","role":"major","firstAppearance":"s22","summary":"First mention: “When the old gentleman had said all he had to say in the way of promise and advice, and Kit had said all he had to say in the way of assurance and thankfulness, he was handed over again to the old lady, who, summoning…”"},{"id":"mr-brass","name":"Mr. Brass","role":"major","group":"g-brass","firstAppearance":"s11","summary":"First mention: “Mr Brass thought that if he did, the Grand Turk’s feelings were by no means to be envied, but he said it was famous, and he had no doubt he felt very like that Potentate.”"},{"id":"mr-quilp","name":"Mr. Quilp","role":"supporting","group":"g-quilp","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: “‘Harkee, Mr Quilp, then,’ pursued the other, ‘You have some influence with my grandfather there.’”"},{"id":"sampson-brass","name":"Sampson Brass","aliases":["Sampson","Mr. Sampson Brass","Mr. Sampson"],"role":"supporting","group":"g-brass","firstAppearance":"s13","summary":"First mention: “Daniel Quilp of Tower Hill, and Sampson Brass of Bevis Marks in the city of London, Gentleman, one of her Majesty’s attornies of the Courts of the King’s Bench and Common Pleas at Westminster and a solicitor of the Hi…”"},{"id":"mrs-quilp","name":"Mrs. Quilp","role":"supporting","group":"g-quilp","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: “‘Ask Mrs Quilp, pretty Mrs Quilp, obedient, timid, loving Mrs Quilp.”"},{"id":"mrs-jarley","name":"Mrs. Jarley","aliases":["Jarley"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s27","summary":"First mention: “‘I am Mrs Jarley.’”"},{"id":"mr-codlin","name":"Mr. Codlin","aliases":["Codlin"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s16","summary":"First mention: “To this Mr Codlin, who had a surly, grumbling manner, replied, as he twitched Punch off the tombstone and flung him into the box, ‘I don’t care if we haven’t lost a farden, but you’re too free.”"},{"id":"mr-chuckster","name":"Mr. Chuckster","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s14","summary":"First mention: “I trace the same current now, flowing through all his quiet and unobtrusive proceedings.--I am about to sign my name, you observe, at the foot of the articles which Mr Chuckster will witness; and placing my finger upo…”"},{"id":"mr-abel","name":"Mr. Abel","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s14","summary":"First mention: “Chuckster, bring in Mr Abel’s articles.’”"},{"id":"miss-brass","name":"Miss Brass","role":"supporting","group":"g-brass","firstAppearance":"s33","summary":"First mention: “The other was his clerk, assistant, housekeeper, secretary, confidential plotter, adviser, intriguer, and bill of cost increaser, Miss Brass--a kind of amazon at common law, of whom it may be desirable to offer a brie…”"},{"id":"mr-garland","name":"Mr. Garland","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s14","summary":"First mention: “I trust, Mr Garland, my dear Sir, that we may mutually congratulate each other upon this auspicious occasion.’”"},{"id":"jacob","name":"Jacob","role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s13","summary":"First mention: “Hold your noise, little Jacob.”"},{"id":"christopher","name":"Christopher","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s21","summary":"First mention: “‘We are here before you, you see, Christopher,’ said Mr Garland smiling.”"},{"id":"nelly","name":"Nelly","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “‘More care!’ said the old man in a shrill voice, ‘more care of Nelly!”"},{"id":"miss-monflathers","name":"Miss Monflathers","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s29","summary":"First mention: “And these audiences were of a very superior description, including a great many young ladies’ boarding-schools, whose favour Mrs Jarley had been at great pains to conciliate, by altering the face and costume of Mr Gri…”"},{"id":"fred","name":"Fred","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “‘Fred!”"},{"id":"mrs-jiniwin","name":"Mrs. Jiniwin","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s4","summary":"First mention: “‘Ah!’ said the spokeswoman, ‘I wish you’d give her a little of your advice, Mrs Jiniwin’--Mrs Quilp had been a Miss Jiniwin it should be observed--‘nobody knows better than you, ma’am, what us women owe to ourselves.’”"},{"id":"mr-witherden","name":"Mr. Witherden","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s14","summary":"First mention: “At first there was a great shaking of hands and shuffling of feet, succeeded by the presentation of the nosegay; for a voice, supposed by the listener to be that of Mr Witherden the Notary, was heard to exclaim a grea…”"},{"id":"mr-cheggs","name":"Mr. Cheggs","aliases":["Cheggs"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s8","summary":"First mention: “But all these sayings and doings and thinkings being unknown to Mr Swiveller, affected him not in the least; he was debating in his mind how he could best turn jealous, and wishing that Sophy were for that occasion on…”"},{"id":"daniel-quilp","name":"Daniel Quilp","role":"minor","group":"g-quilp","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: “It’s not a long one--Daniel Quilp.’”"},{"id":"isaac-list","name":"Isaac List","aliases":["Isaac"],"role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s29","summary":"First mention: “Seven-and-sixpence to me, old Isaac.”"},{"id":"sarah","name":"Sarah","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s33","summary":"First mention: “‘There she is,’ said Quilp, stopping short at the door, and wrinkling up his eyebrows as he looked towards Miss Sally; ‘there is the woman I ought to have married--there is the beautiful Sarah--there is the female who…”"},{"id":"trent","name":"Trent","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s6","summary":"First mention: “‘Here’s Nelly Trent, dear Mrs Quilp,’ said her husband.”"},{"id":"miss-nell","name":"Miss Nell","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “‘Good night, Miss Nell,’ returned the boy.”"},{"id":"miss-sophy","name":"Miss Sophy","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s8","summary":"First mention: “Miss Melissa Wackles was the eldest daughter, Miss Sophy the next, and Miss Jane the youngest.”"},{"id":"mrs-nubbles","name":"Mrs. Nubbles","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s10","summary":"First mention: “‘I hope there are many a great deal better, Kit,’ said Mrs Nubbles; ‘and that there are, or ought to be, accordin’ to what the parson at chapel says.’”"}],"relationships":[{"id":"r1","source":"nell","target":"nelly","weight":13,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":1,"note":"First named together in Ch. 1."},{"at":"s13","type":"together","label":"Often together","weight":13}]},{"id":"r2","source":"kit","t